WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.381
Anotador is a free tool to label any dataset in your browser, one key per item.

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:07.334
Open a file.

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:13.535
This Excel workbook has three sheets, and you can label one of them, or all of them together.

00:00:13.885 --> 00:00:15.668
Choose what the annotator sees.

00:00:15.668 --> 00:00:19.580
The model's verdict stays hidden here, but it is kept in the output.

00:00:19.932 --> 00:00:21.492
Then pick a label set.

00:00:21.492 --> 00:00:29.153
There are 22 presets, from moderation to sentiment and ratings, and every label can be renamed or recolored.

00:00:29.505 --> 00:00:31.057
Type your name and start.

00:00:31.057 --> 00:00:34.782
Each key press labels the item and moves on to the next one.

00:00:37.607 --> 00:00:38.675
Changed your mind?

00:00:38.675 --> 00:00:42.649
The arrow keys take you back, and your progress is saved as you go.

00:00:42.999 --> 00:00:46.238
When you are done, download the labeled CSV.

00:00:51.369 --> 00:00:57.351
It keeps every original column, and adds the label, the annotator and the time spent on each item.

00:00:58.353 --> 00:01:00.023
A CSV works the same way.

00:01:00.023 --> 00:01:05.302
Here, a model's quiz answers are checked with the Correct and Incorrect preset.

00:01:09.458 --> 00:01:14.500
JSON works too, and chat logs show up as conversations, here rated by sentiment.

00:01:19.619 --> 00:01:21.198
Need a second annotator?

00:01:21.198 --> 00:01:25.541
One click makes a single page with the data and the labels inside.

00:01:25.541 --> 00:01:28.239
And the interface also speaks Portuguese.

00:01:28.491 --> 00:01:33.071
Anotador is open source and runs entirely in your browser.

00:01:33.071 --> 00:01:35.361
Try it at anotador.github.io.
